Title: What They Called Recovery
Credit: Animated feature screenplay — scene draft
Author: Christopher Kokkinos
Draft date: 2026-09-28
Status: SC003 direction accepted (DEC-0014); combined pass provisionally accepted

INT./EXT. ELIAS'S BUILDING/CAR PARK - MORNING

A FINAL NOTICE juts from Elias's overfull mailbox. He pushes it back and steps outside. A delivery van, a car with one bad brake light and a terrier pulling at the kerb pass through his field of view. Nothing demands action; he notices anyway. At the next street his hatchback wears a yellow sticker and a wheel clamp.

ELIAS
You have got to be joking.

The permit is visible. The notice names the wrong street. Elias photographs the permit, bay, notice, street sign and clamp before he opens his boot.

He checks the disc and battery of a compact angle grinder. Sparks jump as he cuts only the clamp's replaceable arm. He waits for the disc to stop, places both pieces neatly by the sign and photographs them. The sticker goes into the passenger footwell. The grinder returns to its case with the battery removed.

He starts the reluctant engine and tests the brake before pulling out. His notice to Mac remains in his jacket. A man watches from across the street, but Elias has already gone.
